{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. A domain is cloneable and safe to share between\nexecutions. The following chapters introduce its members one capability at a\ntime.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    type Error: Send;\n    type NodeData: Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync;\n    type NodeContent: NodeContents;\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n\n    fn cache(&self) -> &ValidationCache<Self>;\n    fn node_path(&self, node: &NodeId<Self>) -> NodePath;\n    fn node_content(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n    fn outgoing_edges(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        label: Self::EdgeLabel,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId<Self>>, Self::Error>;\n    fn load_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<Record<Self::NodeData, Self::EdgeLabel>>, Self::Error>> + Send;\n    fn store_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<Self::NodeData, Self::EdgeLabel>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;\n\n    fn project_sources(&self) -> Option<SourceProject<Self>> { ... }\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n    fn source_address(&self, _data: &Self::NodeData) -> Option<OutlineData> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judge the tests adequate for `requirements.sdk.domain`. The requirement says every application domain implements `Domain`. It says a domain is `Clone + Send + Sync`, and it fixes the trait's associated types, bounds, and method signatures. The three default members are the exception: `project_sources`, `source_node` and `source_address` have only signatures here, and the text gives no behaviour for them.\n\n**Main test.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` covers most of the contract.\n- It implements `Domain` for a fixture type, `Relationships`. The fixture uses opaque `NodeData` and `EdgeLabel` types. Its `Error` is `Send` only: it wraps a `Cell` and is not `Sync`, `Debug`, `Clone` or `std::error::Error`. A stricter bound on `Error` would fail to compile there.\n- The generic `check_bounds<G: Domain>` helper asserts these compile-time bounds:\n  - `G: Clone + Send + Sync`\n  - `NodeData: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`\n  - `EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync`\n  - `Error: Send`\n  - `NodeContent: NodeContents`\n  \n  Because the helper is generic, loosening any of these bounds in the trait would break compilation.\n- It checks that the futures returned by `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` are `Send`, through the `send(...)` helper. The fixture error is not `Sync`, so this matters.\n- It calls `node_content`, `node_path`, `outgoing_edges`, `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` with the declared signatures. It asserts their results, including an error from `outgoing_edges`.\n- It asserts that the default `project_sources` returns `None` and that the default `source_node` returns `SourceError::Invalid`.\n\n**Sharing between executions.** Several tests show a domain being shared and used in concurrent executions:\n- `concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces`\n- `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records`\n- `concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads`\n- `shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls`\n\n**Other tests.** `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested`, `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent`, `behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer`, `later_lighter_agent_calls_preserve_the_contexts_existing_trace` and `contexts_render_once_allow_non_send_values_and_hash_exact_prefix_text` use domain implementations through the trait. `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` does the same for the habeas domain.\n\n**Minor observations.**\n- `check_bounds` does not name `Hash` on `NodeData`. Its `identity` helper checks `Clone + Eq + Send + Sync` only. The fixture's `Identity` does derive `Hash`.\n- I do not count this as a gap. The library's own `ValidationCache` interns `NodeData` in an `IndexSet`, so removing `Hash` from the trait would stop the crate compiling, and every test would fail.\n- The default `source_address` returning `None` is not asserted in `contracts.rs`. The habeas domain test in `src/sdk.rs` asserts `None` for non-source nodes, but through its own override. The default's behaviour is specified by the sources requirements (`requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`), not here, so it is outside this subject.\n\nNo `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
